    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 271227\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n527 AM PDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Showers and thunderstorms will be possible late tonight through \n  Tuesday, with favorable conditions for flash flooding in northwest \n  Arizona on Monday and Tuesday.\n\n* Mild weather and warming temperatures are expected during the\n  second half of the week.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Today through Saturday.\n\nThe latest infrared and water vapor satellite imagery show clouds \nstreaming across the Southwestern US from Hurricane Odalys. Moisture \nwill continue to increase across our forecast area, especially areas \nsouth and east of I-15, as Hurricane Polo continues to pull tropical \nmoisture further north. This moisture will result in increased cloud \ncover today, with low chances for virga and sprinkles across the \nMojave Desert this afternoon and evening. Chances for precipitation \nwill increase across our eastern zones overnight as an upper-level \ntrough begins to nudge into the area. Precipitation chances will \nspread across the area on Monday as this trough continues to push \ninto the area; chances for precipitation will continue into Tuesday \nas this low continues to move through the area. The heaviest \nprecipitation is expected in the eastern portions of our forecast \narea where the tropical moisture will overlap with the dynamics from \nthe trough. A Flash Flood Watch remains in effect for Mohave County \nfrom early Monday morning through late Tuesday evening, as this is \nwhere instability will overlap with higher moisture content. \nPrecipitation across the northwestern portions of our forecast area \nwill be lighter, relying primarily on the forcing associated with \nthe trough on Monday. This trough will continue to push through the \narea on Tuesday, resulting in chances for showers and thunderstorms \nlingering into Tuesday afternoon and evening for our eastern zones. \n\nThings will dry out as the trough clears out of the area Wednesday \nonward. Ridging will set up across the Southwestern US with warming \ntemperatures and mild weather expected during the second half of the \nweek. \n&&\n\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Gusty \nsouthwesterly winds expected this afternoon with gust speeds between \n20 and 25 kts. There is a 30 percent chance of gusts to 30 kts. \nLight shower activity expected across the region this afternoon, \nwith best chances of showers in the vicinity of the terminal between \n20Z and 00Z. Gusts will subside after sunset, but southwesterly \nwinds will remain elevated between 8 and 10 kts overnight. SCT-BKN \naoa 15 kft; CIGs down to 10 kft with shower formation overhead.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Gusty southwesterly \nwinds expected this afternoon across the region, with gust speeds \ngenerally between 20 and 30 kts. Light shower activity expected \nacross the region, with showers in the vicinity of Las Vegas Valley \nterminals most likely between 20Z and 00Z... and in the vicinity of \nColorado River Valley terminals from 20Z through the remainder of \nthe TAF period. SCT-BKN aoa 15 kft; CIGs down to 10 kft with shower \nformation overhead.\n&&\n\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Stessman\nAVIATION...Soulat\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
